# W3C ReSpec specification documents.
#
# These are authoring documents that load the ReSpec build tool from
# www.w3.org. That loader is intentionally Subresource-Integrity-free: it is a
# rolling, W3C-hosted tool (a pinned hash would break rendering on every ReSpec
# release) and it is stripped from the exported spec via class="remove", so it
# never ships. This triggers a false positive for
# html.security.audit.missing-integrity, which is also suppressed inline via
# nosemgrep on the loader line; this entry is a belt-and-suspenders fallback.
docs/specs/**/*.html
